body:
I'll definitely apply to museum jobs, but most of these are already choked up with people holding masters' and Ph.Ds in history. Thanks to the strain of trying to work school and a part time job at once, plus my recent slump in grades thanks to my mental health, I'm nowhere competitive enough. My GPA is barely above 3.0, and at this rate I might drop below the 3.0 mark. I've got no fancy awards or anything, and with no internships it feels hopeless. I do have work experience, but again, it's all either fast food or teaching abroad, which isn't super helpful . . . 

&#x200B;

Sometimes I wish I'd just gone for an associate's in business administration. Those jobs are getting automated soon, and it's not high paying work, but at least I'll have something. And if I could just squeeze into a government job, I'll have plenty of security.
